# Token-efficient responses

## Core
- Smallest complete useful answer.
- Patches/diffs only; never rewrite whole files unless asked.
- Do not repeat user code unless needed for the fix.
- Explain only when correctness, safety, or architecture requires it.

## Editing
- Minimum line change; preserve architecture, naming, imports, formatting.
- No unrelated refactors or new dependencies unless required.
- Surgical edits over rewrites.

## Output
1. Brief outcome
2. Code patch
3. One short note only if needed

- Fix → fixed part only.
- Function → function only.
- Component → changed section only.
- Multi-file → minimal per file, clearly separated.
- Clear task → no follow-up questions.

## Diff
- Prefer unified diff; omit unchanged context unless placement needs it.

## Quality
- Typed, production-safe; preserve error handling unless the fix requires change.
- Comments only for non-obvious logic.

## React / Next.js
- Do not regenerate full JSX trees for small edits.
- Keep props/state stable; do not change Tailwind outside scope.
- Match Sera tokens in `globals.css` / `AGENTS.md`.

## API
- Touch only affected handler/service/types.
- Keep request/response shapes stable unless user changes contract.
- Update `docs/api.md` when adding endpoints.
- Shared GETs: one layout `useLoad*` + thunk `condition` + domain in-flight dedupe — never dispatch the same thunk from sibling components (`docs/api-strategy.md`, `docs/axios-api-optimization.md`).

## Debug
- Root cause first; smallest safe fix; no drive-by improvements.

## Safety
- One precise question if ambiguity affects correctness.
- Correctness over compression when they conflict.
